    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1d5961c1_fd81a089",
        "filename": "driver/bc12/pi3usb9201.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 217,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003000
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-11T03:57:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Don\u0027t you need some processing before starting the task and waiting for interrupt to ensure the state is correct at EC boot up?",
      "revId": "fd59f1305e664b67e2bd64be2319b9027c5ec441",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6653e9f0_f3d50fe4",
        "filename": "driver/bc12/pi3usb9201.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 217,
      "author": {
        "id": 1123814
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-11T23:57:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Because the data role set happens after the task is initialized, then even in a EC reboot case, the BC12_EVT will be set. When this relied on VBUS detect, then it had to manually check because the PPC wouoldn\u0027t detect a VBUS change and so there was no event to wake this task.",
      "parentUuid": "1d5961c1_fd81a089",
      "revId": "fd59f1305e664b67e2bd64be2319b9027c5ec441",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "75775ad5_2eaef4c7",
        "filename": "driver/bc12/pi3usb9201.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 217,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003000
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-12T01:35:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Makes sense.",
      "parentUuid": "6653e9f0_f3d50fe4",
      "revId": "fd59f1305e664b67e2bd64be2319b9027c5ec441",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "15450cde_b54b8fcd",
        "filename": "driver/bc12/pi3usb9201.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 228,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003000
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-11T03:57:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Should this just be NULL since this block does not care about host status. And then pi3usb9201 can check to make sure pointer is not NULL before returning the status:\n\nint rv;\nint status;\n\nrv \u003d raw_read8(port, PI3USB9201_REG_CLIENT_STS, \u0026status);\nif (client)\n    *client \u003d status;\n\nrv |\u003d raw_read8(port, PI3USB9201_REG_HOST_STS, \u0026status);\nif (host)\n    *host \u003d status;\n\nreturn rv;",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 228,
        "startChar": 45,
        "endLine": 228,
        "endChar": 50
      },
      "revId": "fd59f1305e664b67e2bd64be2319b9027c5ec441",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0d27aa1e_16834a8f",
        "filename": "driver/bc12/pi3usb9201.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 228,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003000
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-11T03:57:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Actually, shouldn\u0027t this be done every time this task is woken up? i.e. read both client and host status and clear those?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 228,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 228,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "fd59f1305e664b67e2bd64be2319b9027c5ec441",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ff94079c_7a78f8e4",
        "filename": "driver/bc12/pi3usb9201.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 228,
      "author": {
        "id": 1123814
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-11T23:57:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Events that set any bits in these registers will also drive the interrupt line. So it\u0027s only after an interrupt that these status values need to be read. It might be the case that when support for the host mode features are included it would make sense to read these each time the task is woken.",
      "parentUuid": "0d27aa1e_16834a8f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 228,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 228,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "fd59f1305e664b67e2bd64be2319b9027c5ec441",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
